Push direction switch (push method): a testing patch, kept for debugging.  Not adopted: the default "near" is what
the committed code already does, so this only adds the option to push from the other end.

What it does: adds PUSH_END ("near" = the default, the nearer of the two stations facing the block's ends; "far" =
the other one) to config.py and config_check.py, uses it in push.choose_station, plus a unit test.

Why: the push sweep tested both push directions for every middle block, to tell a
direction problem from a block problem.  Useful again whenever the push method is changed or a push fails only from
one side.

To use it:   git apply workfiles/push_end_testing.patch
             then run with --set PUSH_END='far' (or 'near')
Take it out again before committing (git apply -R workfiles/push_end_testing.patch).
Made against the commit that added this file; check with `git apply --check` first.

